portrayed with affable charm by Jorge  Garcia Hurley was the heart and soul of  lost but in his post last fight the  actor has kept a relatively low profile  despite working constantly here's a look  at what he's been up to since bidding  farewell to the island  following his star-making turn on lost  Garcia didn't waste much time booking  his next gigs it should come as no  surprise that those gigs came via his  pal lost co-creator JJ Abrams first up  was a brief but hilariously memorable  turn as a bong wielding security officer  on Abrams underappreciated sci-fi series  fringe you're the best boss I've ever  had Garcia followed that cameo with a  much bigger role on another Abram series  the short-lived crime drama Alcatraz the  show followed a young San Francisco  detective as she tried to unravel the  mystery behind the return of several  long deceased inmates of the infamous  island prison Garcia played dr. Diego  Soto a paranoid conspiracy theorist who  also happens to be an expert on all  things Alcatraz Garcia's comedic chops  have continued to land him roles on  television including a couple of  episodes of one of the biggest sitcoms  of all time How I Met Your Mother he  made his first appearance on the show in  2010 as Steve the Blitz Henry an old  college friend of Marshall and Ted's  much like Hurley the Blitz appears to be  cursed with rotten luck as he got his  nickname because he missed something  amazing every time he left a party early  the episode also makes clever use of  Garcia's lost background by using his  cursed lottery numbers as a phone number  Garcia would reprise the role for  another brief but memorable cameo in the  show's final season when we see that the  blitzes luck hasn't changed all that  much over the years  unlike the Blitz Garcia has had pretty  good luck in his own life as he  continues to book notable supporting  roles on popular TV shows he even went  back to his fantasy roots for ABC's  long-running fairytale drama once upon a  time  Garcia appeared on three episodes of the  show between 2012 and 2013 in a case of  pitch perfect casting he landed the role  of aunt on a magic bean hoarding  surprisingly short giant with a fear of  humans  unfortunately though Garcia didn't share  any screen time with his former lost  co-star Emily de Ravin who was a  once-upon-a-time regular as Belle  Garcia's most surprising cameo came in  2010 when the actors smiling face graced  the cover of Weezer's eighth album the  aptly titled Hurley yes indeed the album  was actually named after Garcia's  beloved lost character as frontman  Rivers Cuomo explained after deciding to  use a photo of Garcia as the cover art  the fans realized that fans would just  refer to it as the Hurley record so it  only made sense to beat them to the  punch  fortunately the album didn't suffer its  name snakes generally rotten luck it  received a warm critical reception and  debuted at number 6 on the Billboard 200  in an even more surprising turn of  events the band even invited Garcia to  come perform live with them on several  tour stops supporting the album and  honestly he wasn't half-bad  Garcia worked hard to make his fans  laugh when he appeared in 2015's the  ridiculous six a Netflix original movie  packed with the likes of Adam Sandler  Rob Schneider and about a dozen or so  other men and women if you've never  heard of ridiculous 6 that's probably  because it wasn't very good in fact it  stands as one of the worst reviewed  films in Adam Sandler's career that  being said  Garcia's turn as the unintelligible herm  was one of the few jokes that actually  worked  although considering the way the movie  was received perhaps he'd rather forget  he was in the movie at all somebody here  could speak her since 2013 Garcia has  portrayed local conspiracy theorists /  consultant Jerry Ortega on CBS's  long-running Hawaii five-o reboot as it  happens it was the idea of a reunion  with his lost co-stars Daniel Dae Kim  and Terry O'Quinn that led Garcia to  take the role the role was initially set  as a 2 episode cameo but Garcia was so  good in the part the producers quickly  promoted him to series regular now he  has no plans on leaving the popular  series anytime soon that's no surprise  considering the perk of shooting on the  island paradise of Oahu which happens to  be where the majority of loss was shot  as well while we're happy that Garcia  has scored some steady work were also a  little worried that he's back on the  island he worked so hard to get away  from
 

